PORT=8080

# All four below are required — the server refuses to start without them
# (see internal/config/config.go). Copy this file to .env and fill in real
# values; .env is gitignored and never committed.

DATABASE_URL=postgres://postgres:admin123@localhost:5432/spotto?sslmode=disable

# Generate with: openssl rand -base64 32
JWT_SECRET=replace-with-a-long-random-string-at-least-16-chars

# AES-256 key for encrypting TOTP (2FA) secrets at rest. Must be exactly 32
# raw bytes, base64-encoded. Generate with: openssl rand -base64 32
TOTP_ENCRYPTION_KEY=replace-with-output-of-openssl-rand-base64-32

CORS_ORIGINS=http://localhost:3000,http://localhost:3001

# Everything below is optional. Leave unset in local dev and the server
# still starts fine — email just logs instead of sending, and Google
# sign-in reports itself as unconfigured instead of failing.

# Base URL of the vendor Next.js app, used to build links embedded in
# emails (invite accept, password reset).
VENDOR_APP_URL=http://localhost:3000

# Base URL of the admin Next.js app — same purpose as VENDOR_APP_URL, but
# for admin-role accounts (e.g. their password-reset email link).
ADMIN_APP_URL=http://localhost:3001

# Public base URL of this API. Traveller password-reset emails link to the
# reset page the API serves at <PUBLIC_API_URL>/reset-password (travellers
# have no web app). Unset: they get the vendor-app link instead.
PUBLIC_API_URL=http://localhost:8080

# Comma-separated list of admin account emails granted the super-admin
# tier (e.g. viewing the cross-admin audit log). Leave unset and every
# admin is shown as a plain "Admin" with no elevated access.
SUPER_ADMIN_EMAILS=

# The deployment's admin account. The API creates it, or corrects its role
# and password, at every boot, so these values are the source of truth:
# change them and redeploy to rotate. Set both or neither. The password
# must be at least 12 characters. ADMIN_EMAIL is also a super-admin.
ADMIN_EMAIL=
ADMIN_PASSWORD=

# development (default) or production. In production the API locks every
# demo/import login (*@spotto.dev, except ADMIN_EMAIL) at boot, and
# cmd/seed and cmd/gendata refuse to run.
APP_ENV=development

# SMTP relay for transactional email (team invites, password reset).
# Works with any SMTP-compatible provider — a Gmail app password, SES
# SMTP credentials, Mailgun SMTP, or Mailtrap for local testing.
SMTP_HOST=
SMTP_PORT=587
SMTP_USER=
SMTP_PASS=
EMAIL_FROM=Spotto <no-reply@spotto.dev>

# Google OAuth client (console.cloud.google.com > APIs & Services >
# Credentials > OAuth client ID > Web application). Redirect URL must be
# registered there and point at this server's /auth/google/callback.
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=
GOOGLE_REDIRECT_URL=http://localhost:8080/auth/google/callback

# Plain API key (console.cloud.google.com > APIs & Services > Credentials >
# API key), not an OAuth client — enable the Calendar API for your project.
# Powers automatic public-holiday closure prompts on the vendor Business
# Profile page. Unset means the holiday scheduler falls back to a bundled
# static Sri Lanka holiday list instead.
#
# The same key (with the Maps JavaScript API + Places API also enabled)
# powers the vendor portal's address-search location picker
# (web/vendor/.env.example's NEXT_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY) and the
# Flutter app's Discover-tab map (app/android/local.properties'
# MAPS_API_KEY) — one Cloud project/key, several config files. It's also
# what internal/placedetails uses for live Places Details lookups (GET
# /places/{id}) that backfill phone/website/wheelchair-accessibility/
# price-level for imported spots — the Places API on this key must have
# billing enabled for that to work; results are cached for 30 days per
# place (see migrations/015_place_details_cache.sql) to keep spend down.
GOOGLE_CALENDAR_API_KEY=

# Tomorrow.io API key (app.tomorrow.io > API Keys) — powers the app's real
# weather (Discover tab bar + Weather screen). Free tier is tight (25
# req/hour, 500/day); the server caches responses for 60 minutes per ~55km
# region to stay well under that. Unset means GET /weather returns 501
# instead of failing startup.
TOMORROW_IO_API_KEY=

# Gemini API key (aistudio.google.com > Get API key) — powers two features:
# (1) BR-certificate OCR pre-fill for vendor Business Registration
# verification (internal/gemini, internal/http/br_cert_scheduler.go). Free
# tier: 10 requests/minute, 250/day, and Google may log/review free-tier
# prompts — fine here since a BR certificate is public-registry data anyway.
# Unset means the br-cert scheduler's OCR sweep is a no-op; vendors can still
# type their certificate number in manually and it still gets verified
# against eROC.
# (2) Local Guide chat + semantic search embeddings (internal/gemini,
# internal/http/guide.go, embedding_worker.go), via Gemini's
# OpenAI-compatibility endpoint. Unset means POST /guide/chat returns 501
# instead of failing startup. This used to be a separate OPENROUTER_API_KEY
# var (internal/openrouter) — that package/var no longer exist, so don't set it.
# Every call is recorded for the admin Local Guide dashboard (tokens, quota,
# real upstream errors, and a "Test connection" button).
GEMINI_API_KEY=
# Optional model overrides. Google retires model ids (gemini-1.5-flash and
# text-embedding-004 both started 404ing), so a retirement is an env change.
# Defaults: gemini-3.5-flash-lite / gemini-embedding-001. Changing the embed
# model makes the embedding worker re-embed every place automatically.
GEMINI_CHAT_MODEL=
GEMINI_EMBED_MODEL=

# Inspiration Board: travellers save a reel (Instagram, TikTok, YouTube) and
# the API watches it with Gemini and lists the places in it.
# GEMINI_VIDEO_MODEL watches the video (defaults to GEMINI_CHAT_MODEL; a
# non-lite Flash model reads on-screen text better).
# GOOGLE_PLACES_API_KEY finds each place worldwide (Places API (New) must be
# enabled, with billing). Falls back to GOOGLE_CALENDAR_API_KEY when blank.
# Found places are kept in the geo_places table and reused.
# YOUTUBE_API_KEY reads YouTube video details (YouTube Data API v3 must be
# enabled on it). Falls back to GOOGLE_PLACES_API_KEY when blank.
# YTDLP_COOKIES_FILE: optional cookies.txt path inside the container (in
# docker-compose: /app/ytdlp/cookies.txt, bind-mounted from /opt/spotto/ytdlp), for
# when Instagram or Facebook refuse anonymous downloads (one cookies.txt can
# hold both). Without the video, places
# come from the caption only.
# INSPIRATION_DAILY_LIMIT: links one traveller can add per 24 hours (default 20).
GEMINI_VIDEO_MODEL=
GOOGLE_PLACES_API_KEY=
YOUTUBE_API_KEY=
YTDLP_COOKIES_FILE=
INSPIRATION_DAILY_LIMIT=

# Cloudflare R2 for image/video uploads. All four are required together to
# enable uploads — leave them unset and the /media endpoints report 501
# (the app still runs, media features are just disabled). Create an R2
# bucket + an API token (Account > R2 > Manage API tokens). The bucket
# should stay private — reads are proxied through this API's own
# GET /media/raw/* route (see internal/http/media.go), not served from a
# public R2/custom domain.
# Browsers upload straight to the bucket, so its CORS policy (R2 > bucket >
# Settings > CORS policy) must allow PUT with a Content-Type header from
# every web app that uploads: the vendor site AND the Command Center (admin),
# e.g. AllowedOrigins ["https://<vendor host>", "https://<admin host>"],
# AllowedMethods ["GET", "PUT", "HEAD"], AllowedHeaders ["Content-Type"].
R2_ACCOUNT_ID=
R2_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
R2_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=
R2_BUCKET=

# Phone verification codes for vendor-portal team members (Account page).
# All optional: a channel left blank logs its codes to the API log (outside
# APP_ENV=production) instead of sending them, and is refused in production.
# SMS to Sri Lankan numbers — text.lk (Developers > API token, plus an
# approved sender ID):
TEXTLK_API_TOKEN=
TEXTLK_SENDER_ID=
# SMS to foreign numbers — Twilio:
TWILIO_ACCOUNT_SID=
TWILIO_AUTH_TOKEN=
TWILIO_FROM_NUMBER=
# WhatsApp — Meta WhatsApp Cloud API with an approved copy-code
# *authentication* template (its code parameter and copy button):
WHATSAPP_PHONE_NUMBER_ID=
WHATSAPP_ACCESS_TOKEN=
WHATSAPP_OTP_TEMPLATE=
WHATSAPP_OTP_TEMPLATE_LANG=en_US
WHATSAPP_API_VERSION=v23.0
# Daily limits on verification codes (separately for Sri Lankan and
# foreign numbers) are set by super-admins on the admin dashboard.

# Audio guide transcripts. The transcriber service (transcriber/) claims
# queued audio from /internal/transcripts with this token. Leave unset and
# no transcripts are queued. Generate with: openssl rand -hex 32
TRANSCRIBER_TOKEN=
